\block{Method: the lab's definitions, unchanged}{
\[ N_s(R)=\frac{2}{n(n-1)}\sum_{i<j\in R}|C_i\cap C_j| \]
\[ Z=\sqrt{N_{rand}}\,\frac{\bar N_s^{\,cuisine}-\bar N_s^{\,rand}}{\sigma_{rand}}=\sqrt{N_{rand}}\;d \]
<% if "F1" in figs %>\begin{center}\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{<< figs.F1 >>}\end{center}<% endif %>
\begin{itemize}
\item Four nulls keep the cuisine's ingredients and recipe sizes: random, frequency, category, frequency\,+\,category. $N_{rand}$ = << n0(F.method.n_rand) >>, so Z = << f(F.method.sqrt_n_rand, 0) >>\,$\times$\,d.
\item Baselines: << n0(E.n_genuine_per_region) >> genuine << E.n_sub >>-recipe samples per region (noise floor) and the copy-mutate model (Tuwani 2019, ranked fitness).
\end{itemize}}

