\block{Tools anyone can use (D4, D5)}{
\textbf{FlavorAudit}: a pip-installable, MIT-licensed library with << F.library.n_modules >> modules and << F.library.n_tests >> tests (incl.\ a regression that reproduces the Fig.\,4 signs); data downloaded on first use.\\[0.3em]
\textbf{FlavorPrint}: paste a recipe and a claimed cuisine; it maps the ingredients, places the recipe's $N_s$ among real recipes, and reports a fidelity percentile, the most likely cuisines, unusual and missing ingredients and a stereotype flag.}

